{
  "dom_id": "step-q71431",
  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "An air compressor moves $\\frac{8}{15}$ gallons of air in four seconds. Find the unit rate of gallons per second.",
  "worked_solution": "To compute the unit rate of gallons per second, we divide the number of gallons, $\\frac{8}{15},$ by the number of seconds, $4$, as follows:   \n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{15}÷4\n$$\n\nDividing a fraction by a whole number is equivalent to multiplying the fraction by the reciprocal of that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8}{15}÷4 & =\\frac{8}{15}÷\\frac{4}{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{15}\\times \\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\times 1}{15\\times 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\times 4}{15\\times 4} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\times \\cancel{4}}{15\\times \\cancel{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit rate in this situation is $\\frac{2}{15}$ gallons per second.",
